  "comment": "Vocabularies for deterministic field classification of captured payment text. Matching is case- and punctuation-insensitive on token boundaries (SRL == S.R.L. == s.r.l), so entries are stored in their bare canonical spelling once. The two lists must stay mutually exclusive — the classifier's field-assignment rule depends on a token never meaning both. 'Bt' (Hungarian betéti társaság) is deliberately absent from legal_forms: it collides with Banca Transilvania's ubiquitous 'BT' abbreviation, and the bank reading wins.",
